course: dictionary
lesson: 5608
title: Lifetime: one life, or a very long time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lifetime is the whole time that a person or animal is alive. «Some friendships last a lifetime» means they can last for the whole of a life, from childhood into old age.
explain: The word can also mean how long a thing lasts or works: «the lifetime of a battery» is the time the battery keeps working. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits, then swap in your meaning to check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes people say «I waited a lifetime!» to mean they waited a very long time. Nobody waits a whole life for a bus, so the feeling in the sentence tells you it means something very long, not a real life.
fact: Lifetime means the whole time a person or animal is alive.
fact: A mayfly has a very short lifetime, while a tortoise has a very long one.
fact: «A once-in-a-lifetime chance» means a rare chance that may never come again.
fact: «In his own lifetime» means while he was still alive.
fact: Phrases like «the trip of a lifetime» tell you that something is very special.
exercise: «Some friendships last a lifetime.» What does lifetime mean here? | A bus timetable | A short visit | A week of school | *The whole time a person is alive
exercise: Ayaan says «the trip of a lifetime» is just a normal trip. What does the phrase suggest? | A trip that happens every week | A trip that is very slow | *A rare and very special trip | A trip by bus
exercise: In «the lifetime of a battery», what does lifetime mean? | The shape of the battery | *The time the battery lasts or works | The price of the battery | A battery shop
test: «Qi Baishi became famous in his own lifetime.» What does this mean? | He became famous in a museum | He became famous after he died | He became famous for his carpentry | *He became famous while he was still alive
test: Which phrase tells you that something happens very rarely? | The lifetime of a mayfly | *Once in a lifetime | A lifetime of work | A tortoise's lifetime
exam: In «I waited a lifetime!», what does lifetime mean? | The whole life of a person | *A very long time | A short wait for a bus | The time a battery works
